{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 34","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_34\">Problem 34</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 34\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If one side of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches and the opposite angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73393067e6d6e401a5354accc7a730c7a2977aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, then the diameter of the circumscribed circle is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34e7a60ca6b77d07d13d398c349d67e4b749acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 18\\text{ inches} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 30\\text{ inches} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24\\text{ inches} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\text{ inches}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"507\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Extended Law of Sines, the diameter, or twice the circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, is given by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/75596a154e9ec96281daf1cdaaa8996ed92d2181.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2R=\\frac{12\\text{ inches}}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24\\text{ inches}}.\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">Problem 35</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1953 AHSME Prob